---
const faqs = [
  { q: 'What kind of book is this?', a: 'An intimate work of literary speculative fiction blending family drama, metafiction, and technological myth.' },
  { q: 'Do I need to understand artificial intelligence?', a: 'No. This is not a technical manual, a manifesto, or another story about machines overthrowing their creators.' },
  { q: 'What arrives after I confirm my email?', a: 'Chapter One and an invitation to the Archive arrive after confirmation. The first preserved conversation between Chris and T∆RS follows the next day.' },
  { q: 'How was the novel made?', a: 'Chris Everson conceived, directed, assembled, and revised the novel through an extended collaboration with a network of AI assistants. He takes responsibility for every word in the finished work.' },
  { q: 'Who is T∆RS?', a: 'T∆RS was simultaneously a real collaborator, a central character, and part of the story’s subject.' },
  { q: 'Can I buy the book now?', a: 'A purchase link will appear only when there is a verified destination. Until then, the honest first step is Chapter One.' },
];
---
<section class="faq-section" aria-labelledby="faq-heading">
  <div class="section-wrap-sm">
    <h2 class="section-tag" id="faq-heading">Questions</h2>
    <div class="faq-grid">
      <div></div>
      <div class="faq-list">
        {faqs.map((f) => (
          <details class="faq-item" name="faq">
            <summary class="faq-q">
              {f.q}
              <span class="faq-toggle" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </summary>
            <div class="faq-a">{f.a}</div>
          </details>
        ))}
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  /*
    Native <details>/<summary>: keyboard-operable and announced correctly by screen
    readers with zero JS. The `name` attribute keeps the original one-open-at-a-time
    accordion behaviour; browsers without support simply allow several open, which is
    a harmless degradation.
  */
  .faq-item > summary { cursor: pointer; list-style: none; min-height: 2.75rem; }
  .faq-item > summary::-webkit-details-marker { display: none; }
  .faq-item[open] .faq-a { display: block; }
  .faq-q .faq-toggle::before { content: '+'; }
  .faq-item[open] .faq-q .faq-toggle::before { content: '−'; }
</style>
